 "summary": "A variable-free notation for computation using only application and a few primitive combinators (S and K suffice, with I = SKK); equivalent in power to the lambda calculus via bracket abstraction, Turing-complete, and used to compile functional languages (Turner's SKI reduction machines).",
 "status": "theoretical",
